","transliteration":"rabbika","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":4,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"and (do) not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":5,"ar":"تَكُن","en_gloss":"be","transliteration":"takun","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":6,"ar":"كَصَاحِبِ","en_gloss":"like (the) companion","transliteration":"kaṣāḥibi","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱلْحُوتِ","en_gloss":"(of) the fish","transliteration":"l-ḥūti","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":8,"ar":"إِذْ","en_gloss":"when","transliteration":"idh","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":9,"ar":"نَادَىٰ","en_gloss":"he called out","transliteration":"nādā","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":10,"ar":"وَهُوَ","en_gloss":"while he","transliteration":"wahuwa","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":11,"ar":"مَكْظُومٌۭ","en_gloss":"(was) distressed","transliteration":"makẓūmun","verse_key":"68:48"},{"pos":12,"ar":"٤٨","en_gloss":"(48)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"68:48"}]},{"verse_key":"68:49","surah":68,"ayah":49,"ar_uthmani":"لَّوْلَآ أَن تَدَٰرَكَهُۥ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ لَنُبِذَ بِٱلْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"if his Lord’s grace had not reached him, he would have been left, abandoned and blameworthy, on the barren shore,","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"لَّوْلَآ","en_gloss":"If not","transliteration":"lawlā","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":2,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"that","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":3,"ar":"تَدَٰرَكَهُۥ","en_gloss":"overtook him","transliteration":"tadārakahu","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":4,"ar":"نِعْمَةٌۭ","en_gloss":"a Favor","transliteration":"niʿ'matun","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":5,"ar":"مِّن","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":6,"ar":"رَّبِّهِۦ","en_gloss":"his Lord","transliteration":"rabbihi","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":7,"ar":"لَنُبِذَ","en_gloss":"surely he would have been thrown","transliteration":"lanubidha","verse_key":"68:49"},{"pos":8,"ar":"بِٱلْعَرَآءِ","en_gloss":"onto (the) naked shore","transliteration":"bil-ʿarāi","verse_key":"68